{"nodes": [{"id": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_pr_15_plus_bp_sensitivity_model", "label": "PR 15+ BP-Based Sensitivity Model (spec)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The primary model is capped at 15-49 by the IR/MR recodes, yet adults 50+ in the PR file have 27.20% prevalence against 8.75% at 15-49, and the primary sample is about 88% female. The PR household-member file covers 1,808,013 adults 15+ with 99.87% BP coverage, so it supports a large-sample BP-based sensitivity analysis on the highest-prevalence age group. The PR model is deliberately a sensitivity analysis, never the deployed model, and it depends on the primary pipeline so there is one modeling implementation."}, {"id": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_pr_feature_table", "label": "Harmonised PR Feature Table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The table mirrors the IR/MR harmonised schema where a concept exists and keeps concepts the PR file lacks as explicit missing values rather than omitting them, so the same training and reporting code consumes it. It adds PR-specific cooking_fuel and cooking_fuel_clean, retains anthropometry where the PR file measures it so a future variant needs no rebuild, and reuses existing cleaning and target helpers. The builder validates required columns and codes and fails loudly. Expected size: 1,808,013 rows, 253,421 positives, 14.02%; 962,219 women and 845,794 men; 516,182 aged 50+ at 27.20% prevalence; 183 transgender respondents excluded because the audit sample and primary model use sex codes 1 and 2."}, {"id": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_default_pr_bp_feature_set", "label": "12-Feature Default PR BP Set and Its Variants", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The default uses female, age, urban, wealth, education, tobacco_any, alcohol_any, systolic_mean, diastolic_mean, bp_readings, bp_high, and bp_medication. Anthropometry is excluded because it is measured only for younger women and men, which would make missingness age- and sex-dependent; state, religion, and social_group are excluded to match the primary model's portability and fairness policy; diet, marital status, children ever born, smoking/smokeless split, and alcohol frequency are absent from the PR file; cooking fuel is reserved for an optional household-SES variant. State, fairness, combined, and cooking-fuel variants test those exclusion decisions."}, {"id": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_split_reuse", "label": "PR Split Reuse of the Primary Cluster Partition", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The PR runs inherit the primary cluster-grouped 20% holdout and 5-fold development CV; overlapping clusters reuse their primary split and fold and PR-only clusters are assigned deterministically with the same seed and stratification, so comparisons are not confounded by a different partition. The split source is recorded as reused_primary, pr_only, or mixed, and leakage assertions cover clusters and households. The 15-49 comparison is the same partition filtered, never re-split."}, {"id": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_comparison_report", "label": "Primary vs PR Side-by-Side Comparison Report", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The report compares sample, feature set (32 vs 12), discrimination, calibration, threshold behaviour, sex and age-band metrics, and PR subgroup gaps across the primary, PR 15-49, and PR 15+ runs. It compares discrimination, calibration, and threshold behaviour rather than raw probability levels because samples and feature sets differ, and it must not claim one model is universally better. The PR 15-49 run isolates the feature-set trade-off while the PR 15+ run adds older adults; it is not a pure ablation because the instruments differ."}, {"id": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_pr_sensitivity_model_card_addendum", "label": "PR Sensitivity Model-Card Addendum", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The addendum documents intended use, sample and feature differences, the age gradient, calibration, threshold, subgroup gaps, label bias, limitations, and non-goals so the analysis cannot be mistaken for the deployed screener or a clinical tool. It must state that PR religion and social group describe the household head, that 183 transgender respondents were excluded, and that the PR model uses neither anthropometry nor diet, while remaining publishable without microdata."}, {"id": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_sample_reconciliation_definition_of_done", "label": "PR Sample Reconciliation and Definition of Done", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/spec.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every count must reconcile before anything is published: feature table 1,808,013 rows / 253,421 positives; BP-valid 15+ 1,805,697 / 253,091; BP-valid 15-49 1,290,219 / 112,898; BP-valid 50+ 515,478 / 140,193. The 2,316 rows without a valid BP pair are excluded from the BP model but retained in the table and described in the audit. Additional done criteria are both PR runs with full artifacts, a comparison report covering sample/feature/overall/calibration/threshold/sex/age-band/subgroup tables, the model-card addendum, all tests passing, and no microdata or model binaries committed."}], "edges": [{"source": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_pr_15_plus_bp_sensitivity_model", "target": "_scratch_primary_model_pipeline_spec_primary_model_training_and_evaluation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_pr_15_plus_bp_sensitivity_model", "target": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_pr_feature_table", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_pr_15_plus_bp_sensitivity_model", "target": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_default_pr_bp_feature_set", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_pr_15_plus_bp_sensitivity_model", "target": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_split_reuse", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_pr_15_plus_bp_sensitivity_model", "target": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_comparison_report", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/spec.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"sourc